WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
What to carry forward.

2
00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:07.363
Read each provider’s documentation for what its models are built to do, and label it as a claim.

3
00:00:07.643 --> 00:00:11.589
Use independent leaderboards to shortlist, knowing what each measures.

4
00:00:11.869 --> 00:00:19.741
Treat data terms and distinctive tools as first-class criteria, because they often decide the question before capability does.

5
00:00:20.021 --> 00:00:31.477
Then decide with a small eval on your task: a rubric written first, a cheap tier included, grading that does not favor any candidate, and a decision made on lower confidence bounds.

6
00:00:31.757 --> 00:00:33.869
Date the decision and keep the eval.

7
00:00:34.149 --> 00:00:39.461
That is the whole of model selection, and it is the first half of this elective’s project.
